<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for April 26.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for April 26.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc announced on Friday the following data and forecasts for natural gas use in the period 24 to 26 April.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 24 (actual) 221 mcm, 52 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 25 (forecast) 233 mcm, 54 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 26 (forecast) 216 mcm, 50 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>Apr 24 (actual) 10.5 Celsius, SNT 10.6 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 25 (forecast) 8.5 Celsius, SNT 10.7 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 26 (forecast) 9.9 Celsius, SNT 10.8 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called on Friday, with none</p>
<p>expected on Saturday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
